    'Solar farm installations require long-range wireless backhauls, solar power systems, trenching, and thermal optics. Our Fort Worth team delivers heavy-duty outdoor security solutions built for renewable energy sites.',
    'We design and install video systems for utility scale solar farms, community solar sites, battery storage yards, substations, and wind and gas energy facilities across Tarrant County and the surrounding North Texas counties, including Wise, Parker, Johnson, Hood, Denton, Erath, and Palo Pinto, with sites reached along I-20, I-35W, US 287, and the rural farm to market roads between them. Because most of these locations have no utility power at the fence, we build self powered thermal and long range assemblies with solar panels, sized battery banks, and cellular or point to point wireless backhaul selected on measured signal at the coordinate rather than on a coverage map. Hardware is specified for hail, straight line wind, blowing dust, and triple digit heat, and locally based technicians handle service calls, seasonal vegetation related repositioning, and same day footage export for a copper theft report.',
